 Respect 12 edit targets, 12 groups/48 operations, 64KB context, 96KB proposal output, 256KB result and 48KB world-definition bounds. Collection maxima do not imply all content fits at once. Narrow/paginate context and batches; report omitted findings. Contradiction/trap diagnostics are bounded analysis, not exhaustive solvability proof.
 
+For top-level foundation additions, select `collection:<owner>:<field>` targets from `list_edit_targets` or Creator's scope list. These append-only scopes carry an exact parent version, item schema and cardinality; they do not include the array or claim the assistant has read its contents. Read/select referenced people, routes, acts and hooks through their ordinary narrow targets. Use `add-item` in the exact collection and `$new:<logical-key>` IDs, including the schema-defined children of new decisions (choices), endings (variants), gates (conditions) and relationship mechanics (bands). Child references require the parent creation group. Complete new records appear in review; Apply is still a draft change. Rediscover generated IDs and prepare ordinary entity edits to revise them later.
+
+The shared allowlist covers Bible's ten ID-record arrays, Routes' six, Endings' two, Mechanics' eight and Creative Direction's `scopedVariations`. It excludes primitive string arrays and protected provenance. Scalar/root edits or individual records that exceed the context budget still require a different supported scope; ceilings are unchanged (exactly 64,000 context, 96,000 proposal and 256,000 result bytes). A collection descriptor does not bypass full-artifact/reference validation, stale-base rejection or whole-foundation approval. Oversized foundation approval reviews may still require Creator.
+
 Place only authorized supplied artwork in the configured local staging directory through the assistant's filesystem tools, or let the user upload through Creator. `list_staged_assets` supplies basenames/digests; `import_staged_asset` creates unapproved candidates. Inspect the actual normalized image, alt text, credit/license and retained approval with asset reads/review before seeking exact approval. Approved replacements do not silently retarget existing scenes/maps. No arbitrary filesystem/URL import or image-generation provider is exposed through MCP.
 
